    "updated_at": "2020-11-24T17:06:57Z",
    "body": "That works.  The other thing I just noticed is that although the newer bash from homebrew was first on my PATH, alacritty was still starting the older /bin/bash as the first shell.  When I forced it to start the homebrew version it does work as expected.  So I think your bash version guess was right on the money.  It's fixed for me now (thank you!!), I leave it to you how much you care about supporting the ancient bash version that ships with even modern Macs.",
