    "updated_at": "2020-11-29T22:49:45Z",
    "body": "I'll try it tomorrow, but I expect the problem to still be present (since\nthat's why I installed the homebrew version in the first place)\n\nOn Sun, Nov 29, 2020, 13:12 Kevin Song <notifications@github.com> wrote:\n\n> I leave it to you how much you care about supporting the ancient bash\n> version that ships with even modern Macs.\n>\n> @dunmatt <https://github.com/dunmatt> We actually explicitly try to keep\n> support for older bashes, specifically because we're one of the only shell\n> frameworks that works for these older shells. (We have some users on\n> Scientific Linux 6 as well).\n>\n> I did a little poking around, and while I can't exactly replicate your\n> issue (maybe because Apple made some minor changes to bash between 10.14\n> and 11.0?), I found that mixing /bin/bash and /usr/local/bin/bash from\n> homebrew does result in inconsistent behavior for SHLVL. You can see that\n> when I switch between the two, SHLVL sometimes doesn't increment and\n> sometimes jumps up by two:\n>\n> The default interactive shell is now zsh.\n>\n> To update your account to use zsh, please run `chsh -s /bin/zsh`.\n>\n> For more details, please visit https://support.apple.com/kb/HT208050.\n>\n>\n>\n> ↕️  1 ~\n>\n> ➜ /usr/local/bin/bash\n>\n>\n>\n> ↕️  1 ~\n>\n> ➜ /usr/local/bin/bash\n>\n>\n>\n> ↕️  2 ~\n>\n> ➜ /usr/local/bin/bash\n>\n>\n>\n> ↕️  3 ~\n>\n> ➜ /usr/local/bin/bash\n>\n>\n>\n> ↕️  4 ~\n>\n> ➜ exit\n>\n>\n>\n> ↕️  3 ~ took 2s\n>\n> ➜ exit\n>\n>\n>\n> ↕️  2 ~ took 4s\n>\n> ➜ exit\n>\n>\n>\n> ↕️  1 ~ took 7s\n>\n> ➜ exit\n>\n>\n>\n> ↕️  1 ~ took 8s\n>\n> ➜ /bin/bash\n>\n>\n>\n> The default interactive shell is now zsh.\n>\n> To update your account to use zsh, please run `chsh -s /bin/zsh`.\n>\n> For more details, please visit https://support.apple.com/kb/HT208050.\n>\n>\n>\n> ↕️  2 ~\n>\n> ➜ /usr/local/bin/bash\n>\n>\n>\n> ↕️  2 ~\n>\n> ➜ /bin/bash\n>\n>\n>\n> The default interactive shell is now zsh.\n>\n> To update your account to use zsh, please run `chsh -s /bin/zsh`.\n>\n> For more details, please visit https://support.apple.com/kb/HT208050.\n>\n>\n>\n> ↕️  4 ~\n>\n> ➜\n>\n>\n>\n> ↕️  4 ~\n>\n> ➜ /bin/bash --version\n>\n> GNU bash, version 3.2.57(1)-release (x86_64-apple-darwin20)\n>\n> Copyright (C) 2007 Free Software Foundation, Inc.\n>\n>\n>\n> ↕️  4 ~\n>\n> ➜\n>\n>\n> So I'm suspecting that somehow, the way that bash 3.2 and bash 5.0 handle\n> SHLVL is inconsistent.\n>\n> If you start alacritty with /bin/bash and then explicitly spawn new copies\n> of /bin/bash (instead of whichever bash is picked up by your PATH), does\n> SHLVL work? If so, I think the issue is that the two shells (3.2 and 5.0)\n> are fundamentally incompatible as far as SHLVL goes, and I'm not sure we\n> can do much on our end aside from warning people that SHLVL isn't\n> consistent when mixing bash versions.\n>\n> —\n> You are receiving this because you were mentioned.\n> Reply to this email directly, view it on GitHub\n> <https://github.com/starship/starship/issues/1909#issuecomment-735447086>,\n> or unsubscribe\n> <https://github.com/notifications/unsubscribe-auth/AAIN7SZGW235EQO4EOPJMNLSSKTJNANCNFSM4T366QBQ>\n> .\n>\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
