    "updated_at": "2020-12-03T23:00:52Z",
    "body": "You might be right--I'm very bad at keeping track of startup file rules (and I swear sometimes they change between platforms).\r\n\r\nSo let me just summarize to make sure I have everything right (`oldbash` is the version that comes with MacOS and `newbash` is the one you get from homebrew):\r\n- When using just `oldbash`, `SHLVL` increments, but `starship` doesn't seem to see it.\r\n- When using `newbash`, everything seems to work as expected.\r\n- When `oldbash` with the `--login` flag, the module works correctly.\r\n\r\nIs this correct?",
