    "created_at": "2020-12-04T16:23:26Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-12-04T16:23:26Z",
    "body": "It's not that simple.  My understanding previously was that simple, so I'm sorry to have mislead you, but I've been digging deeper, and the good news is that **I'm now convinced there's no bug at all**, merely a failure to understand shells on my part!  It all comes down to the `--login` flag.  When a shell is \"logged in\" starship works, when the shell is not \"logged in\" it does not work, behold:\r\n\r\n    ↓1 ~\r\n    ➜ echo $SHLVL\r\n    1\r\n    ↓1 ~\r\n    ➜ echo $SHELL\r\n    /bin/bash\r\n    ↓1 ~\r\n    ➜ /bin/bash --version\r\n    GNU bash, version 3.2.57(1)-release (x86_64-apple-darwin18)\r\n    Copyright (C) 2007 Free Software Foundation, Inc.\r\n    ↓1 ~\r\n    ➜ /bin/bash\r\n    ↓1 ~\r\n    ➜ /bin/bash\r\n    ↓1 ~\r\n    ➜ /bin/bash\r\n    ↓1 ~\r\n    ➜ /bin/bash --login\r\n    ↓5 ~\r\n    ➜ logout\r\n    ↓1 ~\r\n    ➜ echo $SHLVL\r\n    4\r\n    ↓1 ~\r\n    ➜ /bin/bash --login\r\n    ↓5 ~\r\n    ➜ /bin/bash\r\n    ↓5 ~\r\n    ➜ /bin/bash\r\n    ↓5 ~\r\n    ➜ /bin/bash --login\r\n    ↓8 ~\r\n    ➜\r\n\r\nThe reason it appeared to be version dependent before was that I didn't understand Alacritty's default behavior WRT the login flag.  Specifically, I didn't read the comment in the config file that clearly explained that `--login` is default behavior on OSX.  Now, what `--login` actually means?  That I don't know... but you can bet that next time I need to debug a shell thing I'm going to look it up.",
